"A votary is an Artonan sworn to a knight, such as Drusi-otta to Lind-otta."
"Votaries pride themselves on remaining in the shadow, guarding unseen."
"The System has no English for the word and renders it only as votary."
"Votaries are wizards serving as assistants and dedicated casters, often to a single knight."
"They fill education gaps, care for the knight, meet social duties, and may join in the field."
"Knights' spouses in siblingholds are often former votaries and experts in fields of magic."
"The bond binds neither side: a knight may decline a votary, and a votary may change how to serve."
"A votary keeps the knight's secrets eternally and may go on missions as a casting assistant."
"What a votary does is to the patron's credit; a votary stands ready through the patron's moods."
"Student votaries walk campus before sunrise preparing the school, in gray-brown with wooly capes."
"They hold a procession when the sun touches the daystart stone."
"Rapport votaries are above-average wizards who finish education in needed areas and swear to serve."
"Some votaries serve the Rapport through a craft, such as learning-cushion thread enchantment."
"Votaries live among the Rapports and make no fortune."
